      "raw": "Can you believe, I couldn't even remember what time episodes usually drop. XD I've been catching up with 2025's episodes, I have three left as of today.\n\n*What is this intro music??*\n\nI sympathize with Adam, I have also been sitting here the whole time.\n\nOkay, better music. :) I like that little bit of the intro we tend not to get.\n\nThe Disparation rulebook was lying to us? Impossible! Clearly, we got the rulebook from a different universe, it's true there. :P (Also now a collector's item!)\n\nSo glad Trevor is back, too, I knew that from the recent Play Greater Podcast episode. :D\n\nGasp! Crossword issue??? :D Also oh shoot, is this America's Cleverst Legacy happening?\n\nI like what injury is doing to Legacy here, that's not something he's used to, clearly.\n\nHonestly, I am really enjoying actually getting to see how Crossword works, I've kind of never figured that out.\n\nDang, my boy can steal a whole trainload of stuff! :D Go, little guy, you're about to get your butt kicked!\n\nThe Wraith, just rifling through Iron Curtain's Communist underwear!\n\nOh man, hearing the letter song for real feels amazing.\n\n...Oh my god, that's a lot of letters.\n\nCongrats to Striped Burrower for cracking the proverbial champagne bottle over this episode!\n\nAnarchy Past Midnight? XD Is this a reference? Because that name is great.\n\nImagine making Adam read a letter entirely in a bad Australian accent after he hasn't read anything in a year. XD\n\n*Three* letters? Oh my! :O Wonder what I wrote about.\n\nI'm glad this was all a bit. XD\n\nSo Crisis Man's deal is ADHD, got it.\n\nI think I would ship Tyler and Mason. <_< I might have issues. Of comics!\n\nWe're back, baby! :D It feels so good! And I don't think they had to change the outro at all?? Awesome.",
