      "created_at": "2026-05-20T17:59:59.995Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I think it’s more about their own mental state, less about us. (That would have been a funny gag, though. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/grin.png?v=12\" title=\":grin:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":grin:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">)</p>\n<p>Just my opinion, but — based on what they did said — I think they didn’t want to come back to the podcast on a character like Benchmark; they wanted to come back with someone more iconic, more important, as this was very important to them.</p>\n<p>Again, that’s just me extrapolating, though. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/blush.png?v=12\" title=\":blush:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":blush:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
